---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DataBrokerDirectory from '../../components/DataBrokerDirectory';
---

<Layout title="Data Broker Opt-Out Directory" description="Remove your personal information from people-search websites to reduce spear-phishing risks.">
  <div class="bg-indigo-50 py-12 border-b border-indigo-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold text-indigo-900 tracking-tight mb-4">
        Data Broker Opt-Out Checklist
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-indigo-800">
        Companies legally buy and sell your address, phone number, and family connections. Use this checklist to systematically remove yourself from their databases.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <DataBrokerDirectory client:load />

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-12 bg-white border border-slate-200 p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Why is this dangerous?</h3>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        Data Brokers (or "People Search" websites) scrape public records, social media, and purchase data from other companies to build massive profiles on almost every adult in the US and Europe.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        While anyone can pay $5 to find out where you live, the real danger is <strong>Spear-Phishing</strong>. Scammers use this publicly available data to craft highly convincing, personalized emails or phone calls. 
      </p>
      
      <div class="bg-indigo-50 border-l-4 border-indigo-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mt-6">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-indigo-900 mb-2">The Scam Example:</h4>
        <p class="text-indigo-800 text-sm">
          A scammer calls you pretending to be the IRS. Normally you would hang up. But because they looked you up on a data broker site, they can say, "Is this John Smith? We know you live at 123 Main St, and we are about to call your wife, Jane, at her phone number if you don't pay this fine." This weaponizes your public data to cause panic.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
